Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:00.86,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}In this town,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.86,0:00:02.20,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}a giant die rolls
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.20,0:00:03.38,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}every sunrise.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.38,0:00:05.26,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Today, it landed on three.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.57,0:00:06.68,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}All across the plaza,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.68,0:00:08.30,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}people rose off the ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.30,0:00:09.56,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}A baker grabbed his stall
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.56,0:00:11.17,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}as his shoes floated away.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.17,0:00:12.67,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Everyone was rising.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.67,0:00:13.69,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Except Leo.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.69,0:00:14.41,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}He'd tied himself
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.41,0:00:15.61,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}to the clock tower.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.61,0:00:17.13,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Leo hated surprises.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.13,0:00:18.10,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}He even kept a notebook
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.10,0:00:18.94,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}listing what to do
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.94,0:00:19.79,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}if the town suddenly
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.79,0:00:20.98,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}lost gravity.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.98,0:00:22.82,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Every roll changed the law.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.82,0:00:24.55,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}One floated loose objects.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.55,0:00:25.42,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Two made everyone
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.42,0:00:26.32,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}walk backward.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.32,0:00:27.44,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Three lifted people
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.44,0:00:28.34,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}into the air.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.34,0:00:29.47,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}But in thirty years,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.47,0:00:30.32,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}the die had never
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.32,0:00:31.68,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}landed on six.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.68,0:00:33.12,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Leo had counted the rolls.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.12,0:00:33.74,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}And he'd noticed
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.74,0:00:34.93,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}something strange:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.93,0:00:35.52,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}whenever six
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.52,0:00:36.56,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}almost appeared,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.56,0:00:37.15,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}the die made
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.15,0:00:38.87,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}the exact same wobble.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.87,0:00:39.59,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}So while the town
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.59,0:00:40.62,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}floated above him,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.62,0:00:41.63,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Leo slipped underneath
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.63,0:00:42.90,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}the stone platform.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.90,0:00:43.50,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}There was a brass
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.50,0:00:44.74,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}paddle and a crank.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.74,0:00:45.35,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Somebody had been
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.35,0:00:46.02,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}knocking the die
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.02,0:00:47.04,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}away from six before
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.04,0:00:48.03,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}it could settle.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.03,0:00:48.99,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Mayor Pip was holding
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.99,0:00:49.76,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}the handle.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.76,0:00:50.85,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Pip looked ten,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.85,0:00:51.73,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}but he'd started the game
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.73,0:00:53.21,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}thirty years earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.21,0:00:53.87,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Nobody inside
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.87,0:00:55.13,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}the town grew older.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.13,0:00:56.93,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Outside, his family had.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.93,0:00:57.41,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Pip held
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.41,0:00:58.86,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}their faded photograph.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.86,0:01:00.02,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}“If six lands,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.02,0:01:01.08,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}the gate opens,”
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.08,0:01:01.98,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}he whispered.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.98,0:01:02.34,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}“What if they've
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.34,0:01:03.43,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}forgotten me?”
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.43,0:01:04.21,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Leo had an answer
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.21,0:01:05.46,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}for almost everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.46,0:01:06.48,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}But not that.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.48,0:01:07.14,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}He pulled a small
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.14,0:01:08.27,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}pin from the machine,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.27,0:01:09.08,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}stopping the paddle,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.08,0:01:10.89,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}and placed it in Pip's hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.89,0:01:11.95,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}“You can put it back,”
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.95,0:01:12.77,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Leo said.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.77,0:01:13.84,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}“I won't stop you.”
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.04,0:01:14.86,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}The next morning,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.86,0:01:16.65,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}the die didn't land on six.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.65,0:01:17.85,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Neither did the next.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.85,0:01:19.49,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Five mornings went by.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.49,0:01:20.84,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Pip watched each roll,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.84,0:01:21.97,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}holding the pin.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.97,0:01:23.70,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Once, he almost returned it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.70,0:01:24.15,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Then he looked
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.15,0:01:25.02,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}at the photograph
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.02,0:01:26.12,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}and put it down.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.12,0:01:27.51,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}On the sixth sunrise,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.51,0:01:28.91,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}the die began to turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.91,0:01:30.45,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}It rocked toward six.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.45,0:01:31.65,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Pip reached for the pin,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.65,0:01:32.82,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}and stopped himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.82,0:01:33.99,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}The die settled.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.99,0:01:34.91,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Six.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.91,0:01:36.51,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}The town gate swung open.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.51,0:01:37.52,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Pip ran through it,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.52,0:01:38.26,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}past streets
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.26,0:01:39.51,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}he barely recognized,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.51,0:01:40.10,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}until he reached
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.10,0:01:41.13,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}his old house.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.13,0:01:42.02,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}An older woman stood
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.02,0:01:42.94,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}in the doorway.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.94,0:01:44.02,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}She took one look at him
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.02,0:01:45.12,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}and said his name.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.12,0:01:46.45,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Inside was a small chair
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.45,0:01:47.62,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}by the kitchen table.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.62,0:01:48.75,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Everything had changed
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.75,0:01:50.19,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}except that chair.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.19,0:01:51.39,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}“We kept your chair,”
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.39,0:01:52.21,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}she said.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.21,0:01:52.92,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}And Leo,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.92,0:01:54.27,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}watching from the open gate,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.27,0:01:55.72,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}finally closed his notebook
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.72,0:01:57.08,Narr,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}without planning tomorrow.
